lesson.text:
This final set combines the main Hard-level skills:

the argument's structure (a popular account, then challenges, then revision);

abstract headings;

paragraphs that turn midway;

detail and keyword distractors;

headings true of the passage but not of the paragraph.

For each paragraph: (1) note its topic and function, (2) choose the heading that covers the whole paragraph, and (3) check that it is not merely a detail.
